<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Assizes of Romania</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">14th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Assizes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a> is a code of feudal law compiled in the Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaea">Achaea</a> in the first half of the 14th century. It recorded the customs governing the prince, barons and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> of Frankish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> and was later adopted in Venetian possessions in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a>. It preserves cases such as the disputed inheritance of the barony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akova">Akova</a>.</p></div>
